      "writtenOn": "2026-06-30T14:54:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the set of cases here make sense. Structurally, I think the tests should be different.\n\nInstead of directly calling one of the TC run functions, they should set up a fake partner with its CC lines set in a certain way. In the cases where it doesn\u0027t make it to PD, that might be as simple as TCPC emulator call to set CC_STATUS.\n\nOnce we\u0027ve gotten the TC into the appropriate state, the check should be that the port is or is not sourcing VBUS. There shouldn\u0027t be a need to reach in and check the arguments passed to `set_state_tc`.\n\nAs a beneficial side effect, I think that would avoid the need for most of the fakes currently in use.",
      "revId": "2b2665686ff2edc48eb7c4af9f6c942a70f01281",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
